# groot-share-selfhosted — TEMPLATE only. Do not commit real secrets.
#
# DISCLAIMER: use at your own risk. You are responsible for your data, secrets,
# and backups. Maintainers are not liable for loss or misuse. See DISCLAIMER.md.
#
# Canonical operator layout (same idea as gghstats-selfhosted):
#   Keep ALL live config and durable data OUTSIDE this git clone.
#   Updating / git pull on groot-share-selfhosted must never overwrite your settings.
#
# This repository’s own semver is in VERSION at the repository root — bump for
# infra/doc/layout releases, not for app code.
#
# Server / dogfood setup:
#   1. export GFS_HOST_DATA=/home/gfs/gfs-data   # absolute, outside clone
#   2. mkdir -p "$GFS_HOST_DATA"
#      sudo chown 65532:"$USER" "$GFS_HOST_DATA"
#      sudo chmod 2775 "$GFS_HOST_DATA"   # UID 65532 + your user both write (sqlite + .env)
#   3. cp run/common/.env.example "${GFS_HOST_DATA}/.env"
#      chmod 600 "${GFS_HOST_DATA}/.env"
#   4. Edit "${GFS_HOST_DATA}/.env" — set GFS_HOST_DATA to that path
#      and GFS_BOOTSTRAP_* (min 8 chars; no well-known default).
#      Leave GFS_TOPOLOGY=vps unless bucket + AWS_* are filled (vps-s3 fail closed).
#   5. From the clone root:
#        ./run/scripts/compose-stack.sh minimal up -d
#
# What lives under GFS_HOST_DATA (you own this directory):
#   .env                 — secrets, pins, ports (never in git)
#   gfs.db / archives    — created by gfs under /data in the container
#
# Lab-only: you may point GFS_HOST_DATA at this repo’s data/ directory.
# Do NOT put production secrets in the clone.
#
# Upgrading the running container to a new image (compose restart does NOT swap images):
#   1) Set GFS_VERSION in ${GFS_HOST_DATA}/.env
#   2) ./run/scripts/compose-stack.sh minimal pull
#   3) ./run/scripts/compose-stack.sh minimal up -d

# --- Required: host data directory (outside the clone on servers) ---
# Prefer an absolute path, e.g. /home/gfs/gfs-data or /var/lib/gfs
# Must match the directory that holds this .env file.
GFS_HOST_DATA=/home/gfs/gfs-data

# --- App image pin (unrelated to groot-share-selfhosted VERSION) ---
# GFS_IMAGE=ghcr.io/hrodrig/gfs:v0.7.0
GFS_VERSION=v0.7.0

# Published host port (minimal Compose / docker run). Traefik stack does not publish 8080.
GFS_HOST_PORT=8080

# --- gfs contract (https://github.com/hrodrig/groot-share/blob/main/docs/SPECIFICATIONS.md §5) ---
GFS_TOPOLOGY=vps
GFS_DATA_DIR=/data
GFS_LISTEN=:8080
GFS_LOG_FORMAT=json
GFS_LOG_LEVEL=info

# First admin when the user table is empty (min 8 chars). Ignored once users exist.
# After first start, drop GFS_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN and GFS_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD and recreate.
GFS_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN=
GFS_BOOTSTRAP_PASSWORD=
# Display Name (not the login). Empty → gfs default Administrator.
GFS_BOOTSTRAP_ADMIN_NAME=

# Cookie Secure flag. false for http://127.0.0.1 lab; true behind Traefik HTTPS.
GFS_COOKIE_SECURE=false

# Chrome (gfs ≥ v0.5.0). Empty → gfs defaults. Compose passes these through.
# true = white /login (no crate hero / gfs title / favicon).
GFS_LOGIN_SIMPLE=
# App-bar tag (default "archive door"). "-" hides.
GFS_BRAND_SUB=
# Authenticated footer (default family links). "-" hides.
GFS_FOOTER=

# Optional
# GFS_MAX_UPLOAD_BYTES=34359738368
# GFS_KEEP_LAST=20
# GFS_MAX_AGE_DAYS=90
# GFS_RETENTION_EVERY=1h
# GFS_STAGING_GRACE=24h

# --- Traefik stack only ---
# GFS_HOSTNAME=gfs.example.com
# ACME_EMAIL=you@example.com

# --- vps-s3 only (uncomment; fail closed without bucket + AWS_*) ---
# GFS_TOPOLOGY=vps-s3
# GFS_S3_BUCKET=
# GFS_S3_REGION=us-east-1
# GFS_S3_ENDPOINT=
# GFS_S3_PREFIX=captures/
# GFS_S3_PATH_STYLE=true
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
